  "body": "## What changed\n\nThree items from the delta safety read of PR #3284 (#2604):\n\n1. **The tool window's next number.** When you add a tool, the window compares the typed number with the number `AddTool` will give, and queues `SetToolNumber` only when they differ. The window used `tool_numbers::next_free`, which ignores the machine's reserved pockets. With T1 reserved for a probe, a typed 1 queued nothing, and the cutter became T2 with no message. A new function, `tool_numbers::next_free_for`, calls the same allocation as `AddTool` (`tool_reservations::allocate`), and the window uses it. Now a typed 1 goes to `SetToolNumber`, which refuses it by name.\n2. **Every probe pocket is full.** A new probe is still refused (a probe in an ordinary pocket can break the control's probe macros). The refusal now names the pockets and says what to do:\n   `tool 'Probe 2': the probe pockets of <model> (T1) all hold a tool. Delete or renumber the tool in one of these pockets, or reserve one more probe pocket in the machine file`\n3. **Plain words.** A refusal names a `tool_setter` reservation as \"tool setter\", in the app and in the post check of the tool stream. The word \"probe\" does not change, so the tests and agents that match on it still match.\n\nThe decision is in `docs/decisions/3667-tool-reservations.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- New app tests in `crates/app/tests/tool_reservations.rs`: `next_free_for_a_new_tool_matches_add_tool`, `a_probe_with_every_probe_pocket_full_says_what_to_do`, `a_tool_setter_pocket_is_named_in_plain_words`.\n- New UI test `egui_app::tool_number_tests::a_new_tools_typed_number_is_compared_with_the_reserved_aware_allocation`. It fails on `main` and passes with this change.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick`: 29 of 29 steps pass.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe Add tool button in the desktop app was not clicked. The UI test calls the same function that the button calls.\n\nChangelog: The tool window now expects the same tool number that Add tool gives on a machine with reserved pockets, and a full set of probe pockets gets a refusal that says what to do.\nEffort: low\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #3667\n",
